# Starter-kit clean brand rule

`frontend/starter-kit/` is the production-facing surface for
SEOPartnerHub. It MUST read as an original, in-house product. The fact
that its layout primitives originated from a third-party admin template
(Vuexy / Materio / Pixinvent / ThemeSelection / ThemeForest) is an
internal implementation detail and MUST NOT be exposed in code, copy,
branding, links, comments, file names, or assets.

## Forbidden references

In any file under `frontend/starter-kit/**` you MUST NOT add or leave:

- The literal strings `Vuexy`, `vuexy`, `Pixinvent`, `pixinvent`,
  `ThemeSelection`, `themeselection`, `Materio`, `materio`,
  `themeforest.net`, `pixinvent.com`, `themeselection.com`,
  `pixinvent.ticksy.com`, `vuexy-mui-next-demo`,
  `vuexy-mui-nextjs-admin-template`, or any case / prefix / suffix
  variant of these.
- Identifiers (class names, variables, imports, CSS classes, cookies,
  storage keys, env vars, package names) that embed any of the tokens
  above. Examples that MUST be avoided: `VuexyLogo`, `vuexyTheme`,
  `vuexy-mui-next-demo-1`, `vuexy-mui-nextjs-admin-template`,
  `MaterioLayout`, `PixinventFooter`.
- Logo assets, favicons, OG images, illustrations, or SVG marks taken
  from the original template's brand. The brand mark in
  `src/@core/svg/Logo.tsx` and any related logo component MUST be a
  custom, neutral SEOPartnerHub mark.
- Footer copy crediting the template author or vendor
  ("Made with ❤️ by Pixinvent", "by ThemeSelection", "Powered by
  Materio", etc.).
- Outbound links to template documentation, support, demos, license
  pages, "More themes", or marketplace listings — for example
  `themeforest.net/...`, `demos.pixinvent.com/...`,
  `pixinvent.ticksy.com`, `themeselection.com/...`. ANY external link
  in `frontend/starter-kit/**` must point to a generic upstream
  resource (Next.js, MUI, React, Tailwind, TypeScript official docs)
  or to a SEOPartnerHub-owned URL.
- README, JSDoc, or inline comments that describe the project as a
  template ("This is the Vuexy starter kit", "based on the Materio
  layout", "Vuexy admin template", etc.). Describe it as the
  SEOPartnerHub frontend instead.

## Required values

- `themeConfig.templateName` MUST be `SEOPartnerHub`.
- `themeConfig.settingsCookieName` MUST start with `seopartnerhub-`.
- `package.json` `"name"` MUST be `seopartnerhub-frontend` (or another
  `seopartnerhub-*` slug). `"license"` MUST NOT be `Commercial`
  (the upstream template's license); use `UNLICENSED` or the project's
  agreed license.
- The brand SVG in `src/@core/svg/Logo.tsx` MUST be the SEOPartnerHub
  mark. Do not reintroduce the original template's V-shape paths.
- Footer components in
  `src/components/layout/{horizontal,vertical}/FooterContent.tsx` MUST
  render only neutral SEOPartnerHub copyright text and, if needed,
  internal or generic-resource links. No third-party template
  attribution or marketplace links.
- The shared logo component at `src/components/layout/shared/Logo.tsx`
  MUST import the SVG mark under a neutral name (e.g. `BrandLogo`),
  never `VuexyLogo` or any other vendor-named alias.

## Allowed wording

- Refer to the project as `SEOPartnerHub` (or "the SEOPartnerHub
  frontend").
- It is fine to mention the generic upstream stack (Next.js, MUI,
  React, Tailwind, TypeScript) and link to their official docs as
  general resources.
- Cross-references to `frontend/full-version/` for parity guidance
  (per `.cursor/rules/frontend-parity.mdc`) are allowed in rule and
  doc files OUTSIDE `frontend/starter-kit/**`. They MUST NOT appear
  in shipped code or user-visible copy inside the starter-kit.

## Workflow checklist

Before finishing any change under `frontend/starter-kit/**`:

- [ ] Ran a case-insensitive grep over the changed files for
      `vuexy|pixinvent|themeselection|materio|themeforest` and got
      zero matches.
- [ ] No new file, identifier, asset, cookie, storage key, or env var
      embeds a vendor token from the list above.
- [ ] All external links point to generic upstream docs or
      SEOPartnerHub-owned URLs.
- [ ] No template-author attribution was added to footers, about
      pages, or auth pages.
- [ ] Any new logo / favicon / OG image is original or neutral and
      does not carry the upstream template's brand.

## Relationship to frontend-parity rule

`.cursor/rules/frontend-parity.mdc` requires `starter-kit` to mirror
`full-version`'s structure, naming, and component shapes. That rule
still applies. **Brand identity is the deliberate exception to
parity:** never port the template's brand strings, logos, or vendor
links from `full-version` (or anywhere else) into `starter-kit`.
Mirror layout and code; do not mirror brand.
